title: ERC-CUP government negotiations

See this? report a bug!

@erc_player_erc_led
title: ERC-led <span class="generalitat-coalition" data-parties="erc cup" data-summary="Majority government - [+ parlament_coalition_erc_cup_s +]/[+ parlament_s_majority +]"><span style="color: var(--erc); font-style: italic;">Left-Independence</span> <span style="color: var(--cup); font-style: italic;">Government</span></span>
view-if: parlament_coalition_option_erc_cup_gov_visible and player_party = "erc" and erc_parlament_s >= cup_parlament_s
choose-if: parlament_erc_cup_government_available
unavailable-subtitle: [? if parlament_route_erc_cup_block_seats: ERC and the CUP do not have enough seats for a majority. ?][? if parlament_route_erc_cup_block_roadmap: ERC has no active independence roadmap on which to base the coalition. ?][? if parlament_route_erc_cup_block_relations: The CUP does not trust ERC enough to bridge their different independence roadmaps. ?]
on-arrival: {!
    Q.erc_cup_coalition_phase = 1;
    Q.parlament_coalition_push = 0;
    Q.parlament_coalition_cabinet_seats = Q.parlament_coalition_erc_cup_s;
    Q.parlament_coalition_support_seats = Q.parlament_coalition_erc_cup_s;
    Q.parlament_coalition_leader = "erc";
    Q.parlament_coalition_follower = "cup";
    Q.speaker_party = "cup";
    Q.speaker = Q.year < 2017 ? "Julià de Jòdar" : "Vidal Aragonés";
    Q.speaker_gender = "m";
    Q.month_actions += 1;
!}

As the party that will hold the Presidency, ERC will lead the government negotiations. Before we present CUP with our opening cabinet proposal, the new Parlament must elect its Speaker. We are expected to nominate [+ speaker +] (CUP), leaving the Presidency and the position of the Speaker divided between the partners. Retaining both offices would reduce our leverage in the cabinet talks.

- @erc_leader_accept_cup_speaker
- @erc_leader_retain_speaker

@erc_leader_accept_cup_speaker
title: Nominate [+ speaker +] for Speaker
go-to: parlament_coalition_erc_cup_phase_erc_player_erc_led

@erc_leader_retain_speaker
title: Retain the Speakership for ERC
on-arrival: {!
    Q.speaker_party = "erc";
    Q.speaker = Q.year < 2016 ? "Anna Simó" : "Roger Torrent";
    Q.speaker_gender = Q.year < 2016 ? "f" : "m";
!}
go-to: parlament_coalition_erc_cup_phase_erc_player_erc_led

@erc_player_cup_led
title: CUP-led <span class="generalitat-coalition" data-parties="cup erc" data-summary="Majority government - [+ parlament_coalition_erc_cup_s +]/[+ parlament_s_majority +]"><span style="color: var(--cup); font-style: italic;"> Left-Independence</span> <span style="color: var(--erc); font-style: italic;"><span style="color: var(--cup); font-style: italic;">Government</span></span>
view-if: parlament_coalition_option_erc_cup_gov_visible and player_party = "erc" and cup_parlament_s > erc_parlament_s
choose-if: parlament_erc_cup_government_available
unavailable-subtitle: [? if parlament_route_erc_cup_block_seats: ERC and the CUP do not have enough seats for a majority. ?][? if parlament_route_erc_cup_block_roadmap: ERC has no active independence roadmap on which to base the coalition. ?][? if parlament_route_erc_cup_block_relations: The CUP does not trust ERC enough to bridge their different independence roadmaps. ?]
on-arrival: {!
    Q.erc_cup_coalition_phase = 1;
    Q.parlament_coalition_push = 0;
    Q.parlament_coalition_cabinet_seats = Q.parlament_coalition_erc_cup_s;
    Q.parlament_coalition_support_seats = Q.parlament_coalition_erc_cup_s;
    Q.parlament_coalition_leader = "cup";
    Q.parlament_coalition_follower = "erc";
    Q.speaker_party = "erc";
    Q.speaker = Q.year < 2016 ? "Anna Simó" : "Roger Torrent";
    Q.speaker_gender = Q.year < 2016 ? "f" : "m";
    Q.month_actions += 1;
!}

The CUP will hold the Presidency and lead the government negotiations. Its opening institutional proposal gives ERC the Speaker before the CUP presents us with its cabinet offer.

- @parlament_coalition_erc_cup_phase_erc_player_cup_led: Accept [+ speaker +] as Speaker

@cup_player_erc_led
title: ERC-led <span class="generalitat-coalition" data-parties="erc cup" data-summary="Majority government - [+ parlament_coalition_erc_cup_s +]/[+ parlament_s_majority +]"><span style="color: var(--erc); font-style: italic;">Left-Independence</span> <span style="color: var(--cup); font-style: italic;">Government</span></span>
